isOnImage -- tests whether a point lies on the image of a variety
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isOnImage(W, p)
        isOnImage(F, I, p)
  * Inputs:
      * W, a *note pseudo-witness set: PseudoWitnessSet,, a pseudo-witness set
        for $F(V(I))$
      * p, an instance of the type *note Point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,, a
        point in the ambient space of $F(V(I))$
      * F, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, or *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, or *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,,
        specifying a map
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, which is prime, specifying a
        source variety $V(I)$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note MaxThreads: MaxThreads, => ..., default value 1, specifies the
        maximum number of processor threads
      * *note Software: pseudoWitnessSet_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSoftware=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value M2engine, specify software for homotopy
        continuation
      * *note Threshold: pseudoWitnessSet, => ..., default value 5, computes a
        pseudo-witness set for the image of a variety
      * *note Verbose: numericalImageDegree_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value true, display detailed output
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the point $p$
        lies on $F(V(I))$

Description
===========

This method determines if a point in the ambient target space lies on the image
of a variety. This is done via computing a pseudo-witness set for the image.

If a pseudo-witness set has already been computed, then to avoid repetitive
calculation one may run this function with the pseudo-witness set as input.

The following example determines whether a point lies on the Grassmannian
$Gr(2,4)$ of $P^1$'s in $P^3$, under its Pl&uuml;cker embedding in $P^5$.



+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x_(1,1)..x_(2,4)]; I = ideal 0_R;                   |
|                                                                |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F = (minors(2, genericMatrix(R, 2, 4)))_*;                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : W = pseudoWitnessSet(F, I, Repeats => 2, Verbose => false);|
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : q = first numericalImageSample(F, I)                       |
|                                                                |
|o5 = q                                                          |
|                                                                |
|o5 : Point                                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isOnImage(W, q)                                            |
|                                                                |
|o6 = true                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isOnImage(W, point random(CC^1, CC^#F))                    |
|                                                                |
|o7 = false                                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isOnImage(W, point{{1_CC,0,0,0,0,0}})                      |
|                                                                |
|o8 = true                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

