numericalImageSample -- samples general points on the image of a variety
************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        numericalImageSample(F, I, P, s)
        numericalImageSample(F, I, s)
        numericalImageSample(F, I)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, or *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, or *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,,
        specifying a map
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, which is prime, specifying a
        source variety $V(I)$
      * P, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of points on $F(V(I))$
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of points to sample
        in $F(V(I))$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Software: pseudoWitnessSet_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSoftware=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value M2engine, specify software for homotopy
        continuation
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of sample points on $F(V(I)))$

Description
===========

This method computes a list of sample points on the image of a variety
numerically, by calling *note numericalSourceSample: numericalSourceSample,.

If the number of points $s$ is unspecified, then it is assumed that $s = 1$.

One can optionally provide an initial list of points $P$ on $F(V(I))$, which
will then be completed to a list of $s$ points on $F(V(I))$.

The following example samples a point from the twisted cubic. We then
independently verify that this point does lie on the twisted cubic.



+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[s,t];                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {s^3,s^2*t,s*t^2,t^3};                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : p = first numericalImageSample(F, ideal 0_R)             |
|                                                              |
|o3 = p                                                        |
|                                                              |
|o3 : Point                                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : A = matrix{p#Coordinates_{0,1,2}, p#Coordinates_{1,2,3}};|
|                                                              |
|                2         3                                   |
|o4 : Matrix CC    <-- CC                                      |
|              53        53                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : numericalNullity A == 2                                  |
|                                                              |
|o5 = true                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+



Here is how to sample a point from the Grassmannian $Gr(2,4)$ of $P^1$'s in
$P^3$, under its Pl&uuml;cker embedding in $P^5$. We take maximal minors of a
$2 x 4$ matrix, whose row span gives a $P^1$ in $P^3$.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = CC[x_(1,1)..x_(2,4)];                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : F = (minors(2, genericMatrix(R, 2, 4)))_*;                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : numericalImageSample(F, ideal 0_R)                                      |
|                                                                             |
