numericalNullity -- computes numerical kernel dimension of a matrix
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        numericalNullity M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, with real or complex entries
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Precondition => ..., default value false
      * SVDGap => ..., default value 100000
      * *note Verbose: numericalImageDegree_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value false, display detailed output
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, dimension of the kernel of M

Description
===========

This method computes the dimension of the kernel of a matrix with real or
complex entries numerically, via singular value decomposition (see *note SVD:
(Macaulay2Doc)SVD,).

If $\sigma_1 \ge \ldots \ge \sigma_n$ are the singular values of $M$, then to
establish the nullity numerically we look for the largest "significant" gap
between two consecutive singular values, where the gap between $\sigma_i$ and
$\sigma_{i+1}$ is "significant" if the ratio $\sigma_i / \sigma_{i+1}$ exceeds
the value of SVDGap. If a gap is found which is greater than this threshold,
then all singular values after this gap are considered as numerically zero; if
all gaps are less than this threshold, then the matrix is considered
numerically full rank. The default value of SVDGap is $1e5$.

The option Precondition specifies whether the rows of M will be normalized to
have norm $1$ before computing the SVD. This helps reveal nullity if the matrix
is dense (e.g. for a generic interpolation matrix), but not if the matrix is
sparse (e.g. diagonal). The default value is *note false: (Macaulay2Doc)false,.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : numericalNullity(matrix{{2, 1}, {0, 1e-5}}, Precondition => false)|
|                                                                       |
|o1 = 1                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : numericalNullity(map(CC^2,CC^2,0))                                |
|                                                                       |
|o2 = 2                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The option SVDGap may require tuning by the user.

See also
========

  * *note SVD: (Macaulay2Doc)SVD, -- singular value decomposition of a matrix
  * *note numericalRank: (NumericalLinearAlgebra)numericalRank, -- numerical
    rank of a matrix

Ways to use numericalNullity:
=============================

  * "numericalNullity(List,Boolean)"
  * "numericalNullity(Matrix)"
  * "numericalNullity(Matrix,Boolean)"

For the programmer
==================

