numericalSourceSample -- samples a general point on a variety
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        numericalSourceSample(I, W, s)
        numericalSourceSample(I, p, s)
        numericalSourceSample(I, W)
        numericalSourceSample(I, p)
        numericalSourceSample(I, s)
        numericalSourceSample(I)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, which is prime, specifying a
        variety $V(I)$
      * W, a *note witness set: (NAGtypes)WitnessSet,, a witness set for $V(I)$
      * p, an instance of the type *note Point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,, a
        point on the source $V(I)$
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of points to sample
        on the source $V(I)$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Software: pseudoWitnessSet_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSoftware=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value M2engine, specify software for homotopy
        continuation
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of sample points on the source
        $V(I)$
  * Consequences:
      * If $I$ is not the zero ideal, and a sampling function is not specified
        via Software, then a numerical irreducible decomposition of $I$ is
        performed, and cached under I.cache.WitnessSet.

Description
===========

This method computes a list of sample points on a variety numerically. If $I$
is the zero ideal in a polynomial ring of dimension $n$, then an $n$-tuple of
random elements in the ground field is returned. Otherwise, a *note numerical
irreducible decomposition:
(NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)numericalIrreducibleDecomposition_lpIdeal_rp, of
$I$ is computed, which is then used to sample points.

If the number of points $s$ is unspecified, then it is assumed that $s = 1$.

One can provide a witness set for $V(I)$ if a witness set is already known.

In the example below, we sample a point from $A^3$ and then $3$ points from
$V(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - 1)$ in $A^3$.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,z];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : samp = numericalSourceSample(ideal 0_R)                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {{.892712+.673395*ii, .29398+.632944*ii, .025888+.714827*ii}}           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : samp#0                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {.892712+.673395*ii, .29398+.632944*ii, .025888+.714827*ii}             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Point                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = ideal(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - 1);                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : numericalSourceSample(I, 3)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {{.0639312+.363095*ii, .349078+.480802*ii, -1.12512+.169804*ii},        |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {1.824+.510044*ii, -.745985+1.12127*ii, -.080127+1.17155*ii},           |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {.904524-.892533*ii, 1.19581+.66524*ii, .0902927+.13085*ii}}            |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+



As of version 2.2.0 (Nov 2020), it is also possible to specify a custom
sampling function: namely, one can specify the value of the option Software to
be a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)FunctionClosure, which takes in the ideal
$I$ and returns a point.

The following example shows how to sample a point from SO(5, $\mathbb{R}$).



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : n = 5                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = 5                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : R = RR[a_(1,1)..a_(n,n)]                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : A = genericMatrix(R,n,n);                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             5      5                                                        |
|o8 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : I = ideal(A*transpose A - id_(R^n));                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : q = first numericalSourceSample(I, Software => I -> realPoint(I,       |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = q                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : Point                                                                  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Iterations => 100))                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : matrix pack(n, q#Coordinates)                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = | -.514585 -.0590333 -.340792 .739251 .262836  |                       |
|      | .794998  -.127686  -.519368 .270682 .0930521 |                       |
|      | .218364  .714315   .3546    .47793  -.296496 |                       |
|      | .204042  -.603484  .670006  .36953  .0933285 |                       |
|      | .117732  .325223   .198658  -.12356 .908647  |                       |
|                                                                             |
|                 5         5                                                 |
|o11 : Matrix RR    <-- RR                                                    |
|               53        53                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : norm evaluate(gens I, q)                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = .000003403274161595249                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o12 : RR (of precision 53)                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Since numerical irreducible decompositions are done over *note CC:
(Macaulay2Doc)CC,, if $I$ is not the zero ideal, then by default the output
will be a point in complex space (regardless of the ground field of the ring of
$I$).

