realPoint -- samples a real point on a variety
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        realPoint I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, specifying a source variety
        $V(I)$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Initial => ..., default value "random"
      * Iterations => ..., default value 1000
      * Tolerance => ..., default value 1e-10
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note Point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,, a sample
        real point on $V(I)$

Description
===========

This method samples a real point on a variety numerically, using a combination
of the Nelder-Mead simplex method (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelder%E2%80%93Mead_method ) and line search (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Line_search ) with gradient descent. This can be
much quicker than performing a numerical irreducible decomposition.

The option Tolerance specifies a requested error tolerance for the point, with
respect to the generating set of the ideal.

The option Iterations specifies an upper limit on the number of iterations to
run the approximation algorithms. If this value is too low, then the method
will return a point which may not be within the specified error tolerance.

The following example shows how to sample a point from the 4 x 5 funtf variety.



+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (n,r) = (4,5)                                                        |
|                                                                          |
|o1 = (4, 5)                                                               |
|                                                                          |
|o1 : Sequence                                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = RR[x_(1,1)..x_(n,r)]                                             |
|                                                                          |
|o2 = R                                                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = transpose genericMatrix(R,r,n)                                   |
|                                                                          |
|o3 = {-1} | x_(1,1) x_(1,2) x_(1,3) x_(1,4) x_(1,5) |                     |
|     {-1} | x_(2,1) x_(2,2) x_(2,3) x_(2,4) x_(2,5) |                     |
|     {-1} | x_(3,1) x_(3,2) x_(3,3) x_(3,4) x_(3,5) |                     |
|     {-1} | x_(4,1) x_(4,2) x_(4,3) x_(4,4) x_(4,5) |                     |
|                                                                          |
|             4      5                                                     |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I1 = ideal(A*transpose A - (r/n)*id_(R^n));                          |
|                                                                          |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I2 = ideal apply(entries transpose A, row -> sum(row, v -> v^2) - 1);|
|                                                                          |
|o5 : Ideal of R                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : I = I1 + I2;                                                         |
|                                                                          |
|o6 : Ideal of R                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : elapsedTime p = realPoint(I, Iterations => 100)                      |
| -- .743691s elapsed                                                      |
|                                                                          |
|o7 = p                                                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o7 : Point                                                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : matrix pack(5, p#Coordinates)                                        |
|                                                                          |
|o8 = | .722359  .289465  -.295808  .591752  -.454678 |                    |
|     | -.110166 .0700102 .908882   .630235  .0984753 |                    |
|     | .621173  -.330116 -.0305848 .0539234 .866787  |                    |
|     | .283207  .895726  .292392   -.499725 .179584  |                    |
|                                                                          |
|                4         5                                               |
|o8 : Matrix RR    <-- RR                                                  |
|              53        53                                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : norm evaluate(gens I, p)                                             |
|                                                                          |
|o9 = .000005740470289894439                                               |
|                                                                          |
|o9 : RR (of precision 53)                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

